> substitute x = 2 in x^3 - 1
x^3 - 1 with x = 2
  = 7
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> subst x = 2 in x^3 - 1
x^3 - 1 with x = 2
  = 7
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> substitute x = 2, y = 3 in x^2 + y
x^2 + y with x = 2, y = 3
  = 7
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> substitute x = a + 1 in x^2 - 2x + 1
x^2 - 2x + 1 with x = a + 1
  = a^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> subst t = 0 in sin(t) + cos(t)
sin(t) + cos(t) with t = 0
  = 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> substitute z = 3 in z^2
z^2 with z = 3
  = 9
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
